.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
The size a node may take, as the layout engine reads it\&. 

Internal to the layout engine and the node store\&. A host names each of these one at a time, through schultz_node_set_min_size and the two calls beside it; measuring wants all six together, and that is what this is for\&.
.PP
It is not part of the interface on purpose\&. A call that took all six at once could not set one without being handed the other five, so every caller read them back first, and a caller that did not silently replaced settings it had never heard of\&. 
.PP
Definition in file \fBschultz_layout_internal\&.h\fP\&.
